{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And the manna.</b> Scripture recounts the deficient understanding of those who craved, for the manna was like coriander seed and it was easy to gather, and its appearance was white, and further that they could eat it as it was, and also grind it in a mill and make cakes, or pound it and boil it in a pot, and it had an esteemed taste like the cream of oil, and further it would descend on a clean place after the dew washed the surface." "<b>Like coriander seed.</b> Construct state, like נטע שעשועים." "<b>Coriander.</b> Some say according to [the Talmudic view], and some say mustard, from the root גדין. And I do not know."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:17:10.047559288Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}